  "schema_version": "formalization-faithfulness-1",
  "role": "adjudicator",
  "task_id": "LEV-CH01-HETEROGENEOUS-CELL-AVERAGING-CANONICAL-20260908",
  "trigger": [
    "judge classifications differ",
    "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
    "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N01 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "Classify as not-faithful-weaker: Lean does not recover the selected assignment capability, while its conditional conclusion follows from its supplied data and laws. Additional premises reduce applicability; they are not genuine strengthening.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 8 permits cellwise assignment through appropriate averaging without requiring unequal outputs. The elaborated target places hdifferentCellAverages before the entire existential assignment conclusion. D007 supplies the wrapper, and D008 supplies locality and constant preservation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation accurately reconstructs the supplied declaration. Its unresolved concerns arise from the source-to-abstraction relationship, not a mistranslation. Resolve the reverse implication by examining the complete conditional, and retain the failure to recover the source's full applicability.",
      "primary_evidence": "The direct and blind elaborated types have the same quantifier order and four conjuncts. D001, D002, and D007 specify a single-field record; D003, D004, and D008 specify an operation with two bundled laws. These match the blind translation."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Undetermined is unnecessary for the final classification. The uncertain characterization of appropriate averaging does not prevent establishing the reverse logical implication or identifying the additional unequal-average premise. The resulting no/yes implication pair gives not-faithful-weaker under the supplied policy.",
      "primary_evidence": "The methodology classifies lean_implies_source=no and source_implies_lean=yes as not-faithful-weaker. The target's own premises suffice for all its conclusions, whereas printed page 8 does not condition assignment on a pair of unequal averages."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "The binder meanings are determined. Arbitrary parameter types and measurable regions can represent source instances, so abstraction alone is not a defect. However, the quantified averaging-rule type does not certify physical appropriateness, and the explicit unequal-output premise excludes legitimate source cases. C02 therefore fails as a complete source-domain match, without requiring a scalar or geometric specialization.",
      "primary_evidence": "D005, D006, and D009 specify a nonempty indexed measurable partition of a stored domain, with no finite-cardinality requirement. D015-D017 give an arbitrary measurable space and measure. D003, D004, and D008 impose only locality and conditional constant preservation on the operator. Printed pages 7-8 discuss physical material parameters and cell volumes."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "All disputed operator meanings are determined, but the proposed averaging abstraction is insufficient to establish appropriateness. For two selected points s(c), t(c) in each cell and real parameters, A(m, μ, c, f)=2f(s(c))-f(t(c)) satisfies both bundled laws for every measure. It can return a negative value from a strictly positive field. Thus those laws alone certify neither a material-admissible effective value nor a volume-averaging interpretation. This does not assume that the source prescribes an integral or categorically forbids point sampling.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008 requires only Set.EqOn congruence and preservation of globally constant fields on positive finite cells. D021 defines exact pointwise agreement on the cell. D004 is merely the operator projection. Printed page 8 qualifies the averaging as appropriate but provides no formula or sufficient axioms."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N01 unclear",
      "resolution": "The statement retains cell-local dependence and the input/output roles, but does not establish the required connection to appropriate material averaging. N01 fails for that missing connection. A Riemann solver or time-stepping algorithm is not required for the narrowly selected averaging sentence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D008 locality constrains dependence on the field outside a cell, but neither law requires the operator to use volumeMeasure or express model suitability. D001 and D007 store any Parameter without further conditions. The selected sentence on printed page 8 links the assignment specifically to appropriate averaging over the enclosed cell volume."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The theorem constructs an assignment for a supplied rule; it does not assert existence of an appropriate rule. Assuming an averaging procedure is not inherently unfaithful, since the source leaves the procedure unspecified. Here, however, the supplied structure has no adequacy condition and assignment additionally requires unequal outputs. N06 fails as a representation of the full stated capability, without imposing an unsupported integrability or uniqueness requirement.",
      "primary_evidence": "The averagingRule binder precedes the hypotheses and existential assignment. D008 supplies a total operation and its laws, while D007 packages its outputs. Printed page 8 describes availability of cellwise assignment through appropriate averaging and states no uniqueness theorem."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve to yes for the complete conditional proposition. Given its quantified data and hypotheses, set P(c)=CellAveragedMaterialProperty.mk(A(model, volumeMeasure, c, materialParameters)). The first conjunct follows from the projection; locality supplies the second; constant preservation with hpositive and hfinite supplies the third; unequal outputs imply unequal records by projection, supplying the fourth. This derivation requires no assertion that the source supplies the rule or its laws.",
      "primary_evidence": "D007 constructs a record from every Parameter, and D002 returns that parameter. D008 contains precisely the locality and conditional constant laws. The explicit target supplies positive finite measures and an unequal pair. D010, D013, D014, and D018 give ordinary conjunction, equality, existence, and negated equality."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity and the conflicting C12 assessments",
      "resolution": "The hypotheses are satisfiable: take two singleton cells in a two-point measurable space, counting measure, real parameters, a singleton model type, evaluation on each singleton as the rule, and distinct field values. Thus there is no global inconsistency or empty-domain vacuity. Nevertheless, the conclusion is only packaging of supplied outputs and transport of supplied laws. The round-trip nonvacuity observation and the direct packaging concern are both valid, but should not be conflated.",
      "primary_evidence": "D009 permits the two-singleton partition. D008 admits evaluation on singleton cells for all measures. The chosen counting measure gives each cell measure one, and the chosen field satisfies hdifferentCellAverages. D007 requires no further property of the stored value."
    },
    {
      "item": "Reused dependencies, boundary conventions, and remaining semantic checks",
      "resolution": "D011 evaluates the measure through D017; it introduces no hidden averaging semantics. D018 is negated equality and enforces actual unequal outputs, not merely permitted variation. D012 and D019-D025 make the measure premises exactly positive and finite. D026-D040 give ordinary measurable-set membership, exact coverage, and strict set disjointness. These meanings are established from the supplied declarations, independently of reuse provenance. Boundary allocation and positive finite volumes are reasonable modeling conventions, not decisive defects by themselves. Input/output roles remain distinct, and no norm, error, asymptotic, or numerical-precision claim is substituted.",
      "primary_evidence": "The complete inventory supplies D011 as the function projection and D018 as Not (Eq a b). D031 defines disjointness through common lower bounds, with the supplied set instances yielding empty intersection. Printed pages 7-8 specify neither boundary ownership nor analytic averaging conditions; the target contains no error estimate or limiting process."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "As a representation of the selected source capability, the target only supplies assignments after assuming unequal averages and an abstract rule. Heterogeneous fields can have equal averages on all cells, so heterogeneity does not discharge that premise. The theorem gives no assignment conclusion in those source-permitted cases. Its two rule laws also do not establish appropriate material averaging. Deriving an independent unrestricted packaging lemma from the definitions would not restore the missing applicability of this fixed target."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "The entire Lean conditional follows from its own quantified structures and explicit hypotheses: wrap each output, apply the supplied locality and constant-preservation laws, and transport the supplied inequality through the record projection. Consequently it holds under the source context as well. This logical implication does not mean the source asserts the added premises or validates every admitted operator as appropriate averaging."
    }
  },
  "classification": "not-faithful-weaker",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected source passage does not characterize appropriate averaging. It therefore does not settle which additional operator laws or model-specific admissibility conditions would suffice for a faithful abstraction. This uncertainty does not change the established applicability defect or the reverse logical implication."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "reduced-applicability",
      "evidence": "Printed page 8 permits cellwise assignment without requiring different resulting values. The target requires hdifferentCellAverages before every assignment conclusion.",
      "impact": "Equal-average configurations are omitted, including heterogeneous fields whose variation averages out within each cell. The restriction is not genuine theorem strength."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "insufficient-averaging-semantics",
      "evidence": "D008 admits every local constant-preserving operator, including the real-valued extrapolator 2f(s(c))-f(t(c)), which can ignore volume and produce values outside the field's range.",
      "impact": "The declared laws do not establish appropriateness for material averaging; the measure and model arguments alone supply no such guarantee."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "conditional-packaging",
      "evidence": "D007 wraps arbitrary outputs, D008 already supplies the two asserted laws, and the explicit unequal-output premise supplies the final distinction.",
      "impact": "The proposition is nonvacuously satisfiable but its conclusions follow independently of the source capability. This establishes the reverse logical implication without establishing semantic equivalence."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The attached primary-source renderings and exact inline declarations resolve the disagreements without majority voting. The selected claim is the cell-averaging sentence on printed page 8; neighboring reflection and transmission claims are context, not additional required conclusions. The blind reconstruction matches the declaration. The target excludes equal-average cases and does not certify appropriate averaging, while its complete conditional follows directly from the supplied structures and premises. Accordingly the consistent classification is not-faithful-weaker. No tools were used, no target proof was inspected, and no source or rendering hashes were independently recomputed."
}
